cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the RISB method papers listed in the README."
title: "risb-wannier: rotationally invariant slave-boson solver for Wannier90 Hamiltonians"
abstract: >-
  risb-wannier solves the rotationally invariant slave-boson (multi-orbital Gutzwiller)
  saddle-point equations in the embedding formulation for multi-orbital Hubbard models whose
  one-body part is read directly from wannier90_hr.dat (VASP, Quantum ESPRESSO), spinless or
  with spin-orbit coupling. It supports Kanamori, Slater-Condon and arbitrary U_ijkl
  interactions, fully localised-limit double counting, symmetry-adapted R and Lambda, exact-
  diagonalisation embedding, interaction-ramp continuation, one-shot DFT+RISB and a linearised
  charge self-consistency loop, with multi-core parallelism and benchmark checks.
